From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:32:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs42l84: honour the platform volume limit

The DAC volume has its own put handler, which checks a write against
the control's register range only. A machine driver's
snd_soc_limit_volume() ceiling (platform_max) narrows the range that
the info callback reports, but a write above it still reaches the
codec, up to its +12 dB.

Refuse values above platform_max, as snd_soc_put_volsw() does through
soc_mixer_valid_ctl(). Nothing changes without a limit.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit eaefdaa7303573d9919ac95dae5ce23cdf626cf0)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c
index b8c85c5b96..c210a5c400 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c
@@ -102,6 +102,11 @@ static int cs42l84_put_dac_vol(struct snd_kcontrol *kctl,
 	if (vola < mc->min || vola > mc->max || volb < mc->min || volb > mc->max)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	/* A machine driver's snd_soc_limit_volume() ceiling, as the stock volsw put enforces */
+	if (mc->platform_max && (val->value.integer.value[0] > mc->platform_max ||
+				 val->value.integer.value[1] > mc->platform_max))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	ret = snd_soc_component_update_bits(component, CS42L84_FRZ_CTL,
 					    CS42L84_FRZ_CTL_ENGAGE,
 					    CS42L84_FRZ_CTL_ENGAGE);
